{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zqmldwadevwejnzeid2hcyyuupunquomctthhwb2yp45eulkirsa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and fully verified.\n\n## Scope enumeration\n\nThe C library is small: `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` globs `src/lib.c` into one shared lib. `nm -D` on the C `.so` shows exactly **one defined export**:\n\n```\n0000000000001110 T tritanopia      <- only public symbol\n                 U pow@GLIBC_2.29  <- undefined import, not an export\n```\n\n`include/lib.h` confirms this: one type (`cb_rgb_255`) and one function (`tritanopia`). No namespace-renaming macros. The other 5 functions in `lib.c` (`cbRemoveGammaRGB`, `cbNorm`, `cbDenorm`, `cbApplyGammaRGB`, `Tritanopia`) are `static` → internal linkage, so they're translated as private Rust fns. **All 60 lines of C were translated.**\n\n## Files written\n\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — full translation; `tritanopia` is `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\"`, `cb_rgb_255` is `#[repr(C)]`.\n\n## Floating-point fidelity (the hard part)\n\nThe C code deliberately mixes `float` values with **`double`** literals, which triggers C's usual arithmetic conversions. I preserved this exactly rather than naively using `f32` everywhere:\n\n| C expression | Type it evaluates in |\n|---|---|\n| `RGB.R > 0.04045 ? pow(...) : RGB.R / 12.92` | `f64` (double literals), narrowed to `f32` at the cast |\n| `1.055 * pow(RGB.R, 0.4166666666) - 0.055` | `f64`, narrowed to `f32` |\n| `(float)(RGB.R) / 255.f` | `f32` (float literal) |\n| `RGB.R * 255.f + 0.5f` | `f32` |\n| `Tritanopia` matrix rows | `f32`, with C's left-assoc grouping `(a+b)+c` preserved literally |\n\nTwo other details that would silently break byte-identity:\n- **`pow`**: `f64::powf` lowers to a call to the same glibc `pow` the C build links, so no last-bit divergence.\n- **`(unsigned char)float` cast**: outputs go out of `[0,255]` (e.g. down to `-419.2` and up to `269.4`), where the C cast is implementation-defined. I hand-rolled `f32_to_uchar` to mimic x86-64 `cvttss2si` + low-byte truncation, because Rust's `as` **saturates** where C **wraps** — a plain `as u8` would have produced wrong values on out-of-gamut colors. Per instructions, I reproduced the C behavior rather than \"fixing\" it.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- `cargo build --release` — clean, no warnings.\n- Symbol diff C → Rust: **empty**. Rust exports `T tritanopia`.\n- **Exhaustive differential test**: a `dlopen` harness ran all **16,777,216** RGB inputs (2^24, the entire input domain) through both `.so` files: `tested=16777216 mismatches=0`. Repeated against both an optimized (`-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release`) and a default-flags C build — zero mismatches both times.\n\nThe exhaustive pass also confirms the 3-byte struct-by-value/by-return ABI matches, since every field round-trips correctly. No sub-agents were needed for a library this size."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":478,"cache_read_input_tokens":27235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":478,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f5ce107-3c08-4aac-8438-2e4d95c11161","uuid":"e27f1b80-e6bd-4864-a727-061475df1735","timestamp":"2026-08-19T10:42:11.816Z"}
